.TH PUPPETC-COMPILE 1 "January 2026" "puppetc 0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
puppetc-compile \- Puppet manifest compiler and validator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B puppetc-compile
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] <\fIpuppet_file_or_directory\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B puppetc-compile
is a native Puppet manifest compiler that parses Puppet DSL files, evaluates
manifests, and generates catalogs. It can be used for syntax validation,
catalog compilation, and CI/CD integration.
.PP
When a directory is provided, \fBsite.pp\fR will be loaded from the
\fBmanifests/\fR subdirectory and modules will be loaded from the
\fBmodules/\fR subdirectory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Output the parsed AST (Abstract Syntax Tree) as JSON.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-eval
Evaluate the manifest and compile the catalog.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-catalog
Output the compiled catalog as JSON. Implies \fB\-e\fR.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pretty
Output the catalog in human-readable format with colors. Implies \fB\-e\fR.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Write output to FILE instead of stdout.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-modules " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to modules directory. Default: \fB./modules\fR
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-node " " \fINAME\fR
Execute only the specified node definition. Supports regex node matching.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all\-nodes
Execute all literal node definitions. Regex nodes are skipped.
Useful for CI/CD validation.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-facts " " \fIFILE\fR
Load facts from a JSON file. Supports both facter and PuppetDB formats.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-template " " \fITITLE\fR
Display the template output for a file resource with the specified title.
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-hiera\-data " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to Hiera data directory. Default: \fB./data\fR
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-summary
Print a validation summary suitable for CI/CD. Implies \fB\-e\fR.
Exit code: 0 = all nodes OK, 1 = errors found.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-parallel
Process nodes in parallel for faster execution. Requires \fB\-\-all\-nodes\fR.
.TP
.BR \-8 ", " \-\-puppet8
Check Puppet 8 compatibility. Detects deprecated and removed language features
to help migrate from older Puppet versions. Can be used standalone (lint-only)
or combined with \fB\-e\fR to lint and evaluate.
.sp
\fBPhase 1 \- AST checks:\fR
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Removed Hiera 3 functions: \fBhiera()\fR, \fBhiera_array()\fR, \fBhiera_hash()\fR, \fBhiera_include()\fR
.IP \(bu 2
Legacy top-scope fact variables: \fB$::ipaddress\fR, \fB$::fqdn\fR, \fB$::osfamily\fR, etc. (45+ facts mapped to \fB$facts[]\fR replacements)
.IP \(bu 2
Deprecated functions: \fBvalidate_*\fR, \fBis_*\fR, \fBstr2bool\fR, \fBcreate_resources\fR, etc.
.IP \(bu 2
Class inheritance (\fBinherits\fR keyword)
.IP \(bu 2
Import statements
.RE
.sp
\fBPhase 2 \- File scanning:\fR (when input is a directory)
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
ERB templates: \fBscope.lookupvar()\fR, \fBscope['var']\fR, variables without \fB@\fR prefix
.IP \(bu 2
Ruby files: old function API (\fBPuppet::Parser::Functions.newfunction\fR), Ruby 3.x issues (\fBFile.exists?\fR, \fBURI.escape\fR, \fBPSON\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
metadata.json: version constraints incompatible with Puppet 8
.RE
.sp
Exit code is 1 if any errors (removed features) are found.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose/debug output.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.SH NODE EXECUTION
By default, only the \fBdefault\fR node is executed. Use \fB\-\-node\fR to
execute a specific node (supports regex matching), or \fB\-\-all\-nodes\fR
to execute all literal node definitions.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (or all nodes validated successfully in CI mode)
.TP
.B 1
Error (syntax error, compilation failure, or validation errors in CI mode)
.SH EXAMPLES
Validate a manifest file:
.PP
.RS
puppetc-compile \-e site.pp
.RE
.PP
Compile a catalog for a specific node:
.PP
.RS
puppetc-compile \-c \-n webserver1 /etc/puppet
.RE
.PP
Validate all nodes for CI:
.PP
.RS
puppetc-compile \-\-all\-nodes \-\-summary /etc/puppet
.RE
.PP
Output catalog as JSON:
.PP
.RS
puppetc-compile \-c \-o catalog.json /etc/puppet
.RE
.PP
Check Puppet 8 compatibility (manifests + templates + Ruby files):
.PP
.RS
puppetc-compile \-\-puppet8 /etc/puppet
.RE
.PP
Check a single manifest for Puppet 8 issues:
.PP
.RS
puppetc-compile \-\-puppet8 manifests/site.pp
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I manifests/site.pp
Main manifest file when using directory mode.
.TP
.I modules/
Modules directory containing Puppet modules.
.TP
.I data/
Default Hiera data directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR puppetc-server (1),
.BR puppetc-agent (1),
.BR puppet.conf (5)
